# Self-hosted alternative to GitHub Actions: Monday 05:00 America/Chicago (DST-correct via CRON_TZ,
# supported by cronie/vixie-cron on most Linux distributions; if yours lacks it, set the host to
# America/Chicago or use systemd timers with OnCalendar=Mon *-*-* 05:00:00 America/Chicago).
#
# Put the secrets in a file readable only by the service account, e.g. /etc/bd/env (chmod 600):
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
#   ANTHROPIC_MODEL=...
#   BD_USER_AGENT=SEI BD Research ops@yourcompany.com
#   TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL=...            # leave out for dry runs
#   BD_DB_PATH=/var/lib/bd/bd.sqlite
#
# Install with `crontab -e` as the service account:
CRON_TZ=America/Chicago
0 5 * * 1  cd /opt/bd && set -a && . /etc/bd/env && set +a && ./scripts/weekly.sh >> /var/log/bd/weekly.log 2>&1
